[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186188357 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c3e39928-eadb-5eb3-9eda-f3457f0505b4" "question-94546e94-1af9-54e7-9a1b-29fb0570cfc8" "question-a0026095-8676-593f-8d69-3fa08a38ef1b" "question-bade78ae-2b02-5df2-9480-36d57f4806a3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188065 :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\textrm{Var}[X] = 3,$ $\\textrm{Var}[Y] = 0.24,$ and $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y] = 0.2.$ Determine $\\textrm{Var}[X-Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X \\pm Y] = \\textrm{Var}[X] + \\textrm{Var}[Y] \\pm 2\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X - Y] = 3 + 0.24 - 2 \\cdot 0.2 = 2.84.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188359 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-079f02ad-9ee0-58ac-bead-d4394104b125" "question-d139a777-1244-5988-9682-4e7da954d933" "question-af828237-c44f-5a8f-92ae-a55b1aff2b6f" "question-1e6dcf9d-d6cd-51ac-b73d-58cf9701a199"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188067 :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\textrm{Var}[X] = 5,$ $\\textrm{Var}[Y] = 2,$ and $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y] = 3.$ Find $\\textrm{Var}[2X - 5Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX + bY] = a^2\\textrm{Var}[X] + b^2\\textrm{Var}[Y] + 2ab\\,\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X-5Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 5+(-5)^{2}\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =20+50-60 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188360 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-43034259-a22b-5dd7-b48f-a2ed42e0b13d" "question-7c291da1-e168-5e62-8128-2d4c3d94af53" "question-e96228aa-7e46-5ce5-96d2-d22e87559f00"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188068 :question/problem "The joint probability mass function of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ |\n\nFind $\\textrm{Var}[5X+2Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX+bY] = a^2 \\textrm{Var}[X] + b^2 \\textrm{Var}[Y] + 2ab\\,\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm{E}[X^2] - \\textrm{E}[X]^2,\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y] = \\textrm{E}[XY] - \\textrm{E}[X] \\cdot \\textrm{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ | $1$ |\n\nNow, we can find $\\textrm{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space $S_X,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.4+3\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =1.8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.4+{3}^{2}\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =5.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =5.4-{1.8}^{2} \\\\  & =2.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space $S_Y,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.5+2\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.5+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =2-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y].$ We find $\\textrm{E}[XY]$ using the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0\\cdot f(0,0)+0\\cdot 2\\cdot f(0,2)+3\\cdot 0\\cdot f(3,0)+3\\cdot 2\\cdot f(3,2) \\\\  & =0+0+0+6\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =1.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[XY] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =1.2-1.8\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[5X+2Y] & ={5}^{2}\\cdot 2.16+{2}^{2}\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 5\\cdot 2\\cdot (-0.6) \\\\  & =54+4-12 \\\\  & =46.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188361 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e0b47f27-b72b-520b-9e5b-9f7678a818fc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188069 :question/problem "For three random variables $X_1,X_2,$ and $X_3,$ we have the following variances and covariances:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X_1] = 1,   \\qquad\n\\textrm{Var}[X_2] = 3,   \\qquad\n\\textrm{Var}[X_3] = 8   \\qquad\n$$\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}[X_1,X_2] = 2,   \\qquad\n\\textrm{Cov}[X_1,X_3] = 4,   \\qquad\n\\textrm{Cov}[X_2,X_3] = -5   \\qquad\n$$\n\nFind $\\textrm{Var}[5X_1 + 2X_2 + 3X_3].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X_1, \\ldots, X_n$ are random variables, and $a_1, \\ldots, a_n$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}\\left[\\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{n} a_i X_i \\right]\n= \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{n} a_i^2 \\textrm{Var}[X_i] + 2\\sum\\limits_{i <     j} a_i a_j \\textrm{Cov}[X_i,X_j].\n$$\n\nHence, for $n=3$ random variables, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[{a}_{1}{X}_{1}+{a}_{2}{X}_{2}+{a}_{3}{X}_{3}] & ={a}_{1}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]+{a}_{2}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]+{a}_{3}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}] \\\\  & +2{a}_{1}{a}_{2}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]+2{a}_{1}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]+2{a}_{2}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[5{X}_{1}+2{X}_{2}+3{X}_{3}] & ={5}^{2}\\cdot 1+{2}^{2}\\cdot 3+{3}^{2}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & +2\\cdot 5\\cdot 2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 5\\cdot 3\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =25+12+72+40+120-60 \\\\  & =209.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-c3e39928-eadb-5eb3-9eda-f3457f0505b4" :question/id #uuid "c3e39928-eadb-5eb3-9eda-f3457f0505b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-148304" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.64,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=2.56,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.48.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X+Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X+Y]=0.64+2.56+2\\cdot 0.48=4.16.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bb090ab1-dbc9-5b97-ac8f-d7e17a3c0dab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bb090ab1-dbc9-5b97-ac8f-d7e17a3c0dab" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb090ab1-dbc9-5b97-ac8f-d7e17a3c0dab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e97f786f-3f8e-5534-bb52-d041c29138ac" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1447dd96-4c0d-5c24-b2d3-b8448373e4c3" "answer-b36db42d-1df7-5939-8117-91241e0857be" "answer-3480cd1d-522b-51c3-a913-a3671a5b2050" "answer-e97f786f-3f8e-5534-bb52-d041c29138ac" "answer-4fe36719-579c-5bc3-ba9d-1a7681221763"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1447dd96-4c0d-5c24-b2d3-b8448373e4c3" :answer/id #uuid "1447dd96-4c0d-5c24-b2d3-b8448373e4c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b36db42d-1df7-5939-8117-91241e0857be" :answer/id #uuid "b36db42d-1df7-5939-8117-91241e0857be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.68" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3480cd1d-522b-51c3-a913-a3671a5b2050" :answer/id #uuid "3480cd1d-522b-51c3-a913-a3671a5b2050" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.84" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e97f786f-3f8e-5534-bb52-d041c29138ac" :answer/id #uuid "e97f786f-3f8e-5534-bb52-d041c29138ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fe36719-579c-5bc3-ba9d-1a7681221763" :answer/id #uuid "4fe36719-579c-5bc3-ba9d-1a7681221763" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-94546e94-1af9-54e7-9a1b-29fb0570cfc8" :question/id #uuid "94546e94-1af9-54e7-9a1b-29fb0570cfc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-148315" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{7}{4},$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=\\frac{5}{2},$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\frac{3}{4}.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-Y]=\\frac{7}{4}+\\frac{5}{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{11}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-37059df0-2019-5852-bef9-67f5bbc9e447"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-37059df0-2019-5852-bef9-67f5bbc9e447" :answer-field/id #uuid "37059df0-2019-5852-bef9-67f5bbc9e447" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f957552d-c41f-567d-88a0-ad5c32655218" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f957552d-c41f-567d-88a0-ad5c32655218" "answer-481038a8-d449-5b39-8dda-544960d7f632" "answer-bafd273d-ce56-5258-8a54-032916d858c7" "answer-9f578386-a3d2-544b-abed-42030e1016dc" "answer-e9f70f08-c5c2-55d3-9f31-b5f42ea6e420"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f957552d-c41f-567d-88a0-ad5c32655218" :answer/id #uuid "f957552d-c41f-567d-88a0-ad5c32655218" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-481038a8-d449-5b39-8dda-544960d7f632" :answer/id #uuid "481038a8-d449-5b39-8dda-544960d7f632" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bafd273d-ce56-5258-8a54-032916d858c7" :answer/id #uuid "bafd273d-ce56-5258-8a54-032916d858c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f578386-a3d2-544b-abed-42030e1016dc" :answer/id #uuid "9f578386-a3d2-544b-abed-42030e1016dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9f70f08-c5c2-55d3-9f31-b5f42ea6e420" :answer/id #uuid "e9f70f08-c5c2-55d3-9f31-b5f42ea6e420" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188780 :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=7,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=5,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=3.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X+Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X+Y]=7+5+2\\cdot 3=18.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186186960 :answer-field/correct 17592186186964 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-a0026095-8676-593f-8d69-3fa08a38ef1b" :question/id #uuid "a0026095-8676-593f-8d69-3fa08a38ef1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-148310" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=4,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=1,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=1.2.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-Y]=4+1-2\\cdot 1.2=2.6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-98eba2e3-746d-555e-a1fb-96940568baf2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-98eba2e3-746d-555e-a1fb-96940568baf2" :answer-field/id #uuid "98eba2e3-746d-555e-a1fb-96940568baf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cdcc5b9b-7764-5455-a940-4d7a7c70e3d7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d440fa76-ed34-5fa7-ba1a-4299f3912c16" "answer-a81e4ece-d7f2-5c11-822e-db92a71d403c" "answer-cdcc5b9b-7764-5455-a940-4d7a7c70e3d7" "answer-eeac769e-1c7d-5f17-9702-eee8738c6039" "answer-c23cc5cc-232d-50cb-bf03-dcc14216ffbb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d440fa76-ed34-5fa7-ba1a-4299f3912c16" :answer/id #uuid "d440fa76-ed34-5fa7-ba1a-4299f3912c16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a81e4ece-d7f2-5c11-822e-db92a71d403c" :answer/id #uuid "a81e4ece-d7f2-5c11-822e-db92a71d403c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdcc5b9b-7764-5455-a940-4d7a7c70e3d7" :answer/id #uuid "cdcc5b9b-7764-5455-a940-4d7a7c70e3d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eeac769e-1c7d-5f17-9702-eee8738c6039" :answer/id #uuid "eeac769e-1c7d-5f17-9702-eee8738c6039" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c23cc5cc-232d-50cb-bf03-dcc14216ffbb" :answer/id #uuid "c23cc5cc-232d-50cb-bf03-dcc14216ffbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bade78ae-2b02-5df2-9480-36d57f4806a3" :question/id #uuid "bade78ae-2b02-5df2-9480-36d57f4806a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-148307" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{1}{8},$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=\\frac{3}{4},$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\frac{5}{16}.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X+Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X+Y]=\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{3}{4}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{16}=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d797f9f7-f609-5c5e-ba78-717e24c03bac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d797f9f7-f609-5c5e-ba78-717e24c03bac" :answer-field/id #uuid "d797f9f7-f609-5c5e-ba78-717e24c03bac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b17dce6c-5de4-5ce6-8c5a-0647d6a9d350" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6b5b6e8f-5bc3-560d-8885-95ce43bf6cca" "answer-e8d75129-0300-58cb-992b-b2f66d1dd767" "answer-b17dce6c-5de4-5ce6-8c5a-0647d6a9d350" "answer-d00ac744-2b33-547b-8327-668720b71a82" "answer-f787f52b-7c28-5038-948b-07653cdbb173"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b5b6e8f-5bc3-560d-8885-95ce43bf6cca" :answer/id #uuid "6b5b6e8f-5bc3-560d-8885-95ce43bf6cca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8d75129-0300-58cb-992b-b2f66d1dd767" :answer/id #uuid "e8d75129-0300-58cb-992b-b2f66d1dd767" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b17dce6c-5de4-5ce6-8c5a