tituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X-3Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 5+(-3)^{2}\\cdot 11+2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =20+99-48 \\\\  & =71.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186188783 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186186978 :answer-field/correct 17592186186979] ["question-af828237-c44f-5a8f-92ae-a55b1aff2b6f" :question/id #uuid "af828237-c44f-5a8f-92ae-a55b1aff2b6f"] ["question-af828237-c44f-5a8f-92ae-a55b1aff2b6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-148331"] ["question-af828237-c44f-5a8f-92ae-a55b1aff2b6f" :question/problem "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.1,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=0.7,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.2.$ Find $\\text{Var}[7X-4Y].$"] ["question-af828237-c44f-5a8f-92ae-a55b1aff2b6f" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[7X-4Y] & ={7}^{2}\\cdot 0.1+(-4)^{2}\\cdot 0.7+2\\cdot 7\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =4.9+11.2-11.2 \\\\  & =4.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-af828237-c44f-5a8f-92ae-a55b1aff2b6f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-6e79e9c9-3fca-53e4-af45-03318ed7bb0c" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e79e9c9-3fca-53e4-af45-03318ed7bb0c"] ["answer-a9e6b505-6b6f-5ef8-ab62-f5ba3765a1d6" :answer/id #uuid "a9e6b505-6b6f-5ef8-ab62-f5ba3765a1d6"] ["answer-a9e6b505-6b6f-5ef8-ab62-f5ba3765a1d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a9e6b505-6b6f-5ef8-ab62-f5ba3765a1d6" :answer/value "3.3"] ["answer-5ec9220d-acc9-5f8a-b548-2aa15bc850f8" :answer/id #uuid "5ec9220d-acc9-5f8a-b548-2aa15bc850f8"] ["answer-5ec9220d-acc9-5f8a-b548-2aa15bc850f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5ec9220d-acc9-5f8a-b548-2aa15bc850f8" :answer/value "3.8"] ["answer-13b69179-3383-516b-9efb-08040